<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Cloncurry lifts copper production.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cloncurry lifts copper production.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cloncurry Mining Co NL said on Tuesday its fourth quarter copper cathode output rose four percent from the September quarter to 1,554 tonnes.</p>
<p>Cash operating costs in the December quarter averaged under US$0.68 per pound of copper while the average sales price was US$1.11 a pound, the company said.</p>
<p>The copper was sold through commodities trader Glencore UK Ltd to cable wire maker Metal Manufactures Ltd in Port Kembla, New South Wales, Cloncurry said.  </p>
<p>In calendar 1996, the company produced 4,055 tonnes of copper cathode. Copper production commenced at Cloncurry's Great Australia project in Queensland last March.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
